public with sharing class HouseholdService {

    /**
     * Creates a single NPSP Household Account from a list of new contacts and
     * returns the Household Account Id.
     *
     * Every contact in `members` is related to the same newly created Household
     * Account. The first contact in the list becomes the Household's primary
     * contact, which is what drives NPSP's automatic household naming and
     * greeting generation. The Account Name is intentionally left unset so that
     * NPSP can populate it.
     *
     * @param   members   New contacts (no Id, no AccountId) to add to the household.
     * @return            The Id of the newly created Household Account.
     * @throws  IllegalArgumentException when `members` is null or empty, or when
     *          the Household Account record type is not present in the org.
     */
    public static Id createHousehold(List<Contact> members) {

        // Validate input up front.
        if (members == null || members.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                'HouseholdService.createHousehold requires a non-empty list of members.'
            );
        }

        // Resolve the Household Account record type by DeveloperName so that no
        // record type Id is ever hard-coded.
        Map<String, Id> householdRecordTypes = new Map<String, Id>(
            [
                SELECT Id, DeveloperName
                FROM RecordType
                WHERE SobjectType = 'Account'
                  AND DeveloperName = 'HH_Account'
            ]
        );

        if (!householdRecordTypes.containsKey('HH_Account')) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                'The Household Account record type (DeveloperName HH_Account) is not available in this org.'
            );
        }
        Id householdRecordTypeId = householdRecordTypes.get('HH_Account');

        // Create the Household Account WITHOUT setting its Name. NPSP derives the
        // household name and greeting from the primary contact once it is assigned.
        Account household = new Account(RecordTypeId = householdRecordTypeId);
        insert household;

        // Relate every member to the new Household Account and insert them in one
        // bulk-safe DML statement.
        for (Contact member : members) {
            member.AccountId = household.Id;
        }
        insert members;

        // Designate the first member as the primary contact. Changing the primary
        // contact is one of the events that triggers NPSP automatic naming/greeting.
        household.npe01__One2OneContact__c = members[0].Id;
        update household;

        // Re-save the primary contact so NPSP's contact-side household naming logic
        // also runs. This covers orgs where naming is driven by contact changes and
        // is idempotent, so it never creates an extra or empty household.
        Contact primaryContact = members[0];
        primaryContact.AccountId = household.Id;
        update primaryContact;

        return household.Id;
    }
}
```

The failure is that `npsp__Contact_Name__c` is read-only (NPSP maintains it), so it can't be assigned in Apex. Removing those assignments also removes the need for the contact-name query, leaving 3 SOQL and 2 DML.

